{"campaign_id": "fedcc0f3-5435-4aa3-b839-d2c108082481", "completed_at": "2026-10-12T14:46:29Z", "error": null, "id": "M2", "inquiry_id": null, "kind": "measurement", "request": {"description": "Deterministic initial physical-model measurement of the compiled two-joint arm: inspect compiled dynamics and timing, enumerate official-domain analytic IK branches and joint-limit feasibility, compare analytic and compiled Jacobians at reset and bent configurations, and measure bounded ten-physics-step command responses plus zero-control free decay.", "measurements": [{"args": ["--artifact", "campaigns/evaluations/fedcc0f3-5435-4aa3-b839-d2c108082481/initial_model_measurement.json"], "artifact": "campaigns/evaluations/fedcc0f3-5435-4aa3-b839-d2c108082481/initial_model_measurement.json", "instrument": "python_module", "label": "initial-physical-model", "module": "robot_learning.lab.initial_model_measurement"}], "rationale": "The startup decision frontier is whether early work should first resolve plant/control time scales and sampled-data stabilization or instead train for the official inner-radius exposure gap. No candidate exists, so a policy evaluation cannot answer that distinction. This measurement directly tests the consequential model claims: reachability versus limits, rank-one reset authority, compiled masses/inertias/actuator defaults, and command-to-motion/free-decay response. The result will determine whether the next direction is instrumentation/control-oriented or a baseline/coverage training inquiry; it deliberately leaves protected evaluator hold semantics and learned-policy performance unresolved."}, "result": {"measurements": [{"args": ["--artifact", "campaigns/evaluations/fedcc0f3-5435-4aa3-b839-d2c108082481/initial_model_measurement.json"], "instrument": "python_module", "label": "initial-physical-model", "metrics": {"evaluation_artifact": "campaigns/evaluations/fedcc0f3-5435-4aa3-b839-d2c108082481/python-module-M2-1-initial_model_measurement.json", "evalu